 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "`Setoid.countable_quotient_comap_val_iff` (TauCeti/Data/Setoid/Countable.lean:34) yields `(Quotient.mk s '' K).Countable`. Taking its image under `Quotient.lift` and applying `image_comp` produces a composed map that only matches the goal's `fun c => F.typeSpectrum n {c}` up to `Quot.lift` \u03b9-reduction.",
   "file": "TauCeti/ModelTheory/RelationalConfiguration/FragmentType.lean",
   "fix": "Make the identification explicit, e.g. `have : (Quotient.lift _ _ \u2218 Quotient.mk _) = fun c => F.typeSpectrum n {c} := funext fun _ => Quotient.lift_mk _ _ _` and `rw [this] at hC`. Alternatively, factor out a lemma stating that a countable quotient of `Setoid.ker f` restricted to `C` gives countable `f '' C`, and use it here without `Quotient.lift`.",
   "issue": "After `rw [\u2190 image_comp] at hC`, `hC` is about the image of `Quotient.lift (fun c => F.typeSpectrum n {c}) _ \u2218 Quotient.mk _`. The goal, rewritten with `sUnion_image`, is about the image of `fun c => F.typeSpectrum n {c}`. `exact hC.sUnion ...` closes only because the two maps are definitionally equal through the quotient wrapper, and nothing documents this.",
   "line": 276
  }
 ],
